    "findings": [
      "The candy-filled basket and rotated house already have unsuitable crops. Their newly passing fits follow distorted/simplified masks, not faithful motifs.",
      "The blue/silver flower-pot motif becomes more recognizable than the previous fit, but rounded grid corners and false seams remain.",
      "The shaded red/gold checker is almost erased before fitting; its target differs from the RGB classifier on 41.37% of pixels. Better curve search cannot recover absent target detail.",
      "The printed snowflake/tree checker regresses from a useful coarse grid into printed ink shapes; masks differ by 45.01%. Stripes, dots and floral ink remain false cut boundaries.",
      "The star, checker motifs, dragonfly and bird retain broad shapes, but the neural masks round corners, close narrow gaps and change border connections. Lower error against these altered targets is not better source fidelity.",
      "The two stacked-heart examples produce simpler fits, but thin joins and central checkers are altered. These are not counted as verified artwork successes.",
      "All seven unresolved crops remain unresolved; the material-head experiment does not test a new crop finder."
    ]
  },
