    "findings": [
      "Printed-paper error is already 11.17% in the declared synthetic training pool versus 1.91% for plain counterparts, so real-photo domain shift is not the sole cause.",
      "Only 23 of 32 printed views were sampled in 120 updates, with 33 printed draws. Some badly predicted printed views were sampled twice, so unsampled views are not the entire explanation.",
      "The worst scene images include nearby copies of the heart. Direct inspection confirms the labelled central heart remains in place: apparent large shapes are added neighbors, not a demonstrated image/label registration bug.",
      "Scene body IoU is only 69.17%, compared with 99.07% on plain views. Selected-object foreground under neighboring objects remains a separate limitation."
